    "reply": "The designated gene symbol is KRAS [1]. The translated protein functions within the cell as a guanosine nucleotide-binding enzyme [11: \"encodes a protein that is a member of the small GTPase superfamily\"]. Through this molecular activity, the protein operates as a transducer that regulates cell growth cascades [26: \"acts as a molecular switch to persistently stimulate downstream signaling pathways, including cell proliferation and survival\"].\n\n## Small GTPase Superfamily\nThe associated OMIM title is KRAS PROTOONCOGENE, GTPase; KRAS [4]. At the enzymatic level, this gene specifies a protein belonging to a conserved hydrolase class [11: \"encodes a protein that is a member of the small GTPase superfamily\"]. Alternative pre-mRNA splicing generates",
